preConditionHook:
// EL: avgRange = average(high - low, avgRangeLookback)[1] -- the mean bar
// range over the avgRangeLookback bars ending ONE BAR AGO, so the signal bar
// is not in its own benchmark. Same indexed-Average idiom LargeOutsideBar
// uses.
//
// Average recomputes from scratch every bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808),
// and high - low is a price expression with real history, so this is a FRESH
// loop over price -- not the WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator and not a
// mirrored variable buffer. Summed newest-first, EL's Summation order.
//
// Not NarrowRangeBar: that one's window INCLUDES the current bar (so an
// oversized signal bar raises its own benchmark) and it is a fraction, not a
// multiple. Not BarRangeAboveStd, whose band is mean + K standard deviations
// over a zero-filled variable history and which fires in the LARGER sense --
// negating it gives a different band, since the sd term moves with the
// volatility of volatility.
avgRange = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)avgRangeLookback; ++i) {
    avgRange += high[1 + i] - low[1 + i];
}
avgRange /= (int)avgRangeLookback;
